<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia working days lost to strikes rises.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia working days lost to strikes rises.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of working days lost in Australia due to industrial disputes increased to 51,700 in November from 33,900 in October, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The number of disputes fell to 50 from 63, but the number of employees involved jumped to 48,800 from 22,900, the bureau said.  </p>
<p>The highest number of days lost were in the coal mining industry, which lost 18,800 and education, health and community services, which lost 16,800.</p>
<p>The total number of working days lost for the year to November were 908,000, compared with 588,800 in the previous 12 months, the bureau said.</p>
<p>-- Canberra bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
